1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,963
Reports show what happened in your contact center:

2
00:00:03,963 --> 00:00:06,714
calls, queues, and the time your agents spend.

3
00:00:06,714 --> 00:00:10,312
This video shows where the reports are, how to run one, how to

4
00:00:10,312 --> 00:00:14,015
filter it, what the main numbers mean, how to export it, and the

5
00:00:14,015 --> 00:00:16,290
limits on reports about agents' time.

6
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:23,274
A busy afternoon is an impression.

7
00:00:23,274 --> 00:00:25,122
A manager needs a number:

8
00:00:25,122 --> 00:00:29,890
how many calls came in, how many were missed, and how long callers waited.

9
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:35,532
Reports answer those questions for the whole center, for one queue, or for

10
00:00:35,532 --> 00:00:38,100
one agent, over any period you pick.

11
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:43,321
Every report is worked out from what the platform recorded about each call

12
00:00:43,321 --> 00:00:47,680
and each agent's state, so a total always matches the records behind it.

13
00:00:51,895 --> 00:00:54,440
Open Reports in the admin menu.

14
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:58,911
The page lists every report as a card, grouped by category:

15
00:00:58,911 --> 00:01:06,271
Agent Performance, Billing and Usage, Compliance and Audit, Executive, Operations, Queue and Routing,

16
00:01:06,271 --> 00:01:09,710
Technical and IT, and Workforce and Payroll.

17
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:13,355
CRM and Campaigns holds the reports of the CRM.

18
00:01:13,833 --> 00:01:17,323
In the menu, each category opens to its reports.

19
00:01:17,323 --> 00:01:20,813
You see only the reports your permissions allow.

20
00:01:22,413 --> 00:01:28,579
Contact Center reports need the View Contact Center reports permission, which the Supervisor

21
00:01:28,579 --> 00:01:30,781
and Administrator roles have.

22
00:01:30,781 --> 00:01:34,053
The CRM reports need View Omnichannel reports.

23
00:01:34,803 --> 00:01:41,098
The reports come with the Reports feature and Contact Center Work Distribution.

24
00:01:41,098 --> 00:01:44,727
Excel and PDF export are two more features:

25
00:01:44,727 --> 00:01:47,763
Reports, OpenXml, and Reports, PDF.

26
00:01:52,057 --> 00:01:54,570
Open Operations, Call insights.

27
00:01:54,570 --> 00:01:59,189
A report page has a filter panel on top and the results below.

28
00:01:59,189 --> 00:02:02,517
Each report shows only the filters it uses.

29
00:02:02,975 --> 00:02:05,097
Date range starts on Today.

30
00:02:05,097 --> 00:02:06,705
Click it to choose.

31
00:02:06,705 --> 00:02:09,984
Relative days run from Today to Last 90 Days.

32
00:02:09,984 --> 00:02:13,520
Calendar periods run from This Week to Last Year.

33
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:17,635
Rolling months cover the last three, six or twelve months.

34
00:02:18,162 --> 00:02:24,309
Custom Range takes a start and an end date and time, in the site's time zone.

35
00:02:24,309 --> 00:02:28,382
On or before and On or after leave one side open.

36
00:02:28,926 --> 00:02:31,594
Choose Last 7 Days and click Show.

37
00:02:31,594 --> 00:02:37,398
The cards fill in with total, inbound and outbound calls, answered, abandoned and

38
00:02:37,398 --> 00:02:40,466
failed, then the daily trend below them.

39
00:02:44,683 --> 00:02:49,962
This report offers Queue group, Queue, Agent, Direction and Channel.

40
00:02:49,962 --> 00:02:55,313
A filter left on All does not narrow the report, and filters combine.

41
00:02:55,770 --> 00:03:00,528
Pick the Customer care queue group and the Inbound direction, then click Show.

42
00:03:00,528 --> 00:03:05,230
Every number and percentage is worked out again from only the matching calls.

43
00:03:05,728 --> 00:03:08,548
Pick an Agent to see one person's calls.

44
00:03:08,548 --> 00:03:11,798
Clearing a filter brings the full picture back.

45
00:03:16,059 --> 00:03:19,818
The Executive performance dashboard shows the main numbers.

46
00:03:19,818 --> 00:03:22,594
Interactions counts every call or message.

47
00:03:22,594 --> 00:03:27,741
Inbound offered counts the inbound ones, and Inbound answered counts those an agent

48
00:03:27,741 --> 00:03:30,169
took, with the answer rate under it.

49
00:03:30,773 --> 00:03:36,073
Abandoned is a caller who hung up while waiting, or while an agent was ringing.

50
00:03:36,073 --> 00:03:39,877
Its percentage is abandoned divided by inbound offered.

51
00:03:39,877 --> 00:03:46,113
Voicemail and Callback requested are neither answered nor abandoned, so each has its own card.

52
00:03:46,729 --> 00:03:50,285
Failed is a call that failed for a technical reason.

53
00:03:50,285 --> 00:03:55,066
Average speed of answer is how long inbound callers waited for an agent.

54
00:03:55,066 --> 00:03:59,909
Average handle time is the talk, hold and wrap-up time of a handled call.

55
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:04,728
Transfer rate is the share of answered calls that were transferred.

56
00:04:04,728 --> 00:04:09,653
Recording coverage is the share of answered voice calls that have a recording.

57
00:04:09,653 --> 00:04:14,637
Charts below show the daily trend, the channel mix, each queue's service level,

58
00:04:14,637 --> 00:04:16,338
and the busiest agents.

59
00:04:20,638 --> 00:04:22,780
Open the Export menu:

60
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:26,431
Export CSV, Export Excel and Export PDF.

61
00:04:26,431 --> 00:04:31,749
With only the Reports feature, the button is just Export CSV.

62
00:04:31,749 --> 00:04:36,908
An export uses the same date range and filters as the page.

63
00:04:37,503 --> 00:04:39,577
CSV is one table of data.

64
00:04:39,577 --> 00:04:43,927
Excel puts each section of the report on its own worksheet.

65
00:04:43,927 --> 00:04:48,543
PDF lays the report out as it looks on screen, with its charts.

66
00:04:52,765 --> 00:04:57,206
Reports on agents' time read every state change of every agent.

67
00:04:57,206 --> 00:05:04,220
These are all the Workforce and Payroll reports, plus Agent presence audit and Agent activity timeline.

68
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:07,695
Here is Agent time summary for the last 30 days.

69
00:05:08,171 --> 00:05:12,495
To keep them fast, they cover at most 31 days at a time.

70
00:05:12,495 --> 00:05:15,355
Choose Last 90 Days and click Show.

71
00:05:15,355 --> 00:05:20,376
The report says This period is too long for this report, names the

72
00:05:20,376 --> 00:05:23,375
longest period, and shows no figures.

73
00:05:23,375 --> 00:05:27,351
Other Contact Center reports accept up to 400 days.

74
00:05:27,808 --> 00:05:31,585
Go back to a shorter period and the figures return.

75
00:05:31,585 --> 00:05:33,904
An export has the same limit.

76
00:05:33,904 --> 00:05:38,807
On screen, Agent presence audit lists the most recent 5,000 changes:

77
00:05:38,807 --> 00:05:42,518
pick an agent or a shorter period to see the rest.

78
00:05:46,718 --> 00:05:51,941
With the Report Subscriptions feature, any of these reports can be emailed every

79
00:05:51,941 --> 00:05:55,159
day, week or month from Reports, Subscriptions.

80
00:05:55,159 --> 00:05:59,107
Reports made in the Report Builder cannot be subscribed to:

81
00:05:59,107 --> 00:06:02,508
a workflow with the Email Report task sends those.

82
00:06:06,708 --> 00:06:12,621
On Monday morning, a supervisor opens the Executive performance dashboard for Last Week,

83
00:06:12,621 --> 00:06:17,528
checks the abandonment rate, and exports the PDF for the weekly meeting.

84
00:06:18,278 --> 00:06:23,247
A planner opens Hour-of-day performance for Last 30 Days to see when callers

85
00:06:23,247 --> 00:06:26,338
arrive, and schedules agents for those hours.

86
00:06:27,088 --> 00:06:33,518
Payroll runs the Reconciled payroll timecard one month at a time, and exports it to Excel.

87
00:06:34,268 --> 00:06:40,408
A manager picks one queue and checks its service level before changing how that queue overflows.

88
00:06:42,408 --> 00:06:47,811
Pick a range, set the filters, read the cards, and export what you need.

89
00:06:47,811 --> 00:06:50,997
Keep reports on agents' time to 31 days.

90
00:06:50,997 --> 00:06:52,798
Thanks for watching.

